{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:16:26.599528", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is based on a scalable SDN spine-leaf topology. It consists of:\\n- **Leaf switches**: leaf_1, leaf_2, leaf_3, leaf_4\\n- **Spine switches**: spine_1, spine_2\\n- **Hosts**: host_1_1 to host_4_4\\n- **Controller**: SDN controller at 20.0.0.100\\n- **Subnets**:\\n  - Host subnet: 10.0.0.0/24\\n  - Management subnet: 20.0.0.0/24\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Reachability Test Results**:\\n   - The ping results between hosts indicate that all tests have a status of \"unknown.\"\\n   - No packets were transmitted (`tx`), received (`rx`), or lost (`loss_percent`).\\n   - RTT (Round Trip Time) metrics such as average, minimum, maximum, and deviation are all null.\\n   - This suggests that there is no communication between the hosts.\\n\\n2. **Potential Anomalies**:\\n   - The absence of any reachability data between hosts is abnormal. In a properly functioning network, hosts within the same subnet or across subnets should be able to communicate.\\n   - The \"unknown\" status for all tests may indicate:\\n     - A failure in the SDN controller\\'s configuration or operation.\\n     - Issues with OpenFlow rules on the switches.\\n     - Problems with the physical or logical connectivity between devices.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nTo further diagnose the root cause, the following areas need investigation:\\n1. **SDN Controller**:\\n   - Verify the controller\\'s status and its ability to manage switches.\\n   - Check OpenFlow rules and flow entries on the switches.\\n\\n2. **Switches**:\\n   - Inspect the configuration and operational status of leaf and spine switches.\\n   - Ensure proper connectivity between switches and hosts.\\n\\n3. **Hosts**:\\n   - Validate the network configuration of hosts (IP addresses, routes, etc.).\\n   - Check for any issues with host interfaces.\\n\\n4. **Links**:\\n   - Examine the physical and logical links between devices for any failures.\\n\\n#### Summary\\nThe network is experiencing a complete communication failure between hosts. The root cause is yet to be determined, but the issue likely lies in the SDN controller, switch configurations, or connectivity. Further analysis is required to pinpoint the exact problem., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='cbbde200-dcbe-4c78-8b5d-cf7616453e4e'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
